  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Focus HIV-instrument</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme aims to contribute to strengthen civil society to contribute to the elimination of HIV as a public health threat by 2030. It will focus on adolescent girls and young women from the ages of 15 to 29 and Key population starting from the age of 18.  The programme has 2 main subgoals: (1) Increase access to HIV-services
and integrate people-centered HIV-services in health systems and (2) Strengthen development and implementation of data-informed HIV- and AIDS-policies. This will cover 6 countries in Southern Africa, namely: Angola, Eswatini, Mozambique, South Africa, Zambia and Zimbabwe. Additionally, it will cover the bordering areas of Malawi and Lesotho.</narrative>
  </description>
